Licences of the components in wine.app

Each component, its licence, where its licence texts are in this bundle, and where its source is. SOURCE (beside this
file) names the exact inputs this bundle was built from: upstream commits, the hash of the MacNeutron patch series
applied to each tree ("dev" for a tree built with unexported work), and the source tarballs' URLs and SHA-256. The
patches and pins are in the MacNeutron repository (https://github.com/chadouming/MacNeutron), at the commit SOURCE's
MACNEUTRON_COMMIT names. NOTICES.md quotes the notices that live only in source headers. Not legal advice.

Wine 11.19 (the loader, wineserver, Wine's libraries and programs)
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later. Texts: wine/LICENSE, wine/COPYING.LIB, wine/AUTHORS; Wine's vendored libraries are
  listed in wine/NOTICES.md, and GSM (wine/gsm-COPYRIGHT) and FAudio (zlib licence, wine/faudio-LICENSE) carry their
  own texts. msync (patch 0015) and its helpers adapted from Apple's xnu (APSL-2.0): NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine.git at WINE_COMMIT (tag wine-11.19), with the patches in the
  repository's wine-arm64/patches/wine (pinned in wine-arm64/pins).

FEX (libarm64ecfex.dll and libarm64ecfex.so: runs x86_64 code)
  Licence: MIT, fex/LICENSE; MacNeutron's patches to it are MIT too. Compiled-in externals, each with its text in
  fex/: fmt (MIT), xxhash (BSD-2-Clause), tiny-json (MIT), unordered_dense (MIT), rpmalloc (0BSD), cephes (BSD),
  range-v3 (Boost Software Licence 1.0), cpp-optparse (MIT). SoftFloat-3e (BSD-3-Clause), the VIXL utilities
  (BSD-3-Clause), musl and Arm's routines (MIT) and Madeira's patches (MIT grant): NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://github.com/FEX-Emu/FEX.git at FEX_COMMIT with its submodules at the FEX_SUBMODULE_* commits, and
  the patches in the repository's wine-arm64/patches/fex (pinned in wine-arm64/pins).

DXMT (the Direct3D to Metal DLLs in ../DXMT/aarch64-windows, winemetal.dll and winemetal.so)
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later. Texts: ../DXMT/LICENSE, ../DXMT/COPYING.LIB, ../DXMT/LICENSE.OLD (MIT, for releases up
  to v0.80). DXBCParser (MIT, Microsoft) and the constexpr GUID parser (MIT): NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://github.com/chadouming/dxmt.git at DXMT_COMMIT (../DXMT/version names it too) with its submodules
  at the DXMT_SUBMODULE_* commits, and the patches in the repository's wine-arm64/patches/dxmt (pinned in dxmt/pins).

LLVM 15.0.7 (linked statically into winemetal.so)
  Licence: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception, llvm/LICENSE.TXT; its regular-expression code, llvm/COPYRIGHT.regex;
  ConvertUTF (Unicode, Inc.) and the regex notice: NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project.git at LLVM_TAG (llvmorg-15.0.7), unmodified.

llvm-mingw 20260908 (the Windows-side toolchain: DXMT's DLLs, winemetal.dll and libarm64ecfex.dll link its runtime)
  Licence: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception, llvm-mingw/LICENSE.TXT; the mingw-w64 runtime,
  llvm-mingw/COPYING.MinGW-w64-runtime.txt.
  Source: https://github.com/mstorsjo/llvm-mingw/releases/download/20260908/llvm-mingw-20260908-ucrt-macos-universal.tar.xz
  (SHA-256 LLVM_MINGW_SHA256, pinned in dxmt/pins); the sources it is built from are listed at
  https://github.com/mstorsjo/llvm-mingw.

FreeType 2.14.3 (libfreetype.6.dylib: text rendering in win32u and dwrite)
  Licence: the FreeType License (FTL), elected from FreeType's FTL-or-GPL-2.0 choice. Texts: freetype/LICENSE.TXT,
  freetype/FTL.TXT. Built without PNG, HarfBuzz or Brotli; it links the system's zlib and bzip2. The BDF and PCF
  drivers (X11-style licence): freetype/bdf-README, freetype/pcf-README; its hashing code (MIT-style): NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://download.savannah.gnu.org/releases/freetype/freetype-2.14.3.tar.xz (SHA-256 FREETYPE_SHA256),
  unmodified, pinned in the repository's wine-arm64/deps.pins and built by wine-arm64/build.sh.

gnutls 3.8.13 (libgnutls.30.dylib: TLS for secur32's schannel, PFX import and export for crypt32)
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, gnutls/COPYING.LESSERv2, as is the libtasn1 it includes. The libunistring it includes is
  LGPL-3.0-or-later: gnutls/COPYING.LESSERv3 and gnutls/COPYINGv3 (the GPL-3.0 text the LGPL-3.0 builds on). The
  aarch64 CRYPTOGAMS routines (BSD-3-Clause), gnutls/cryptogams-license.txt; inih (BSD-3-Clause),
  gnutls/inih-LICENSE.txt; randomart (BSD-2-Clause, OpenBSD): NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://www.gnupg.org/ftp/gcrypt/gnutls/v3.8/gnutls-3.8.13.tar.xz (SHA-256 GNUTLS_SHA256), unmodified,
  pinned and built as FreeType is, with nettle and GMP linked in statically.

nettle 4.0 (linked statically into libgnutls.30.dylib)
  Licence: LGPL-3.0-or-later, elected from nettle's LGPL-3.0-or-later or GPL-2.0-or-later choice. Texts:
  nettle/COPYING.LESSERv3, nettle/COPYINGv3.
  Source: https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/nettle/nettle-4.0.tar.gz (SHA-256 NETTLE_SHA256), unmodified, pinned and built as
  FreeType is.

GMP 6.3.0 (linked statically into libgnutls.30.dylib)
  Licence: LGPL-3.0-or-later, elected from GMP's LGPL-3.0-or-later or GPL-2.0-or-later choice. Texts:
  gmp/COPYING.LESSERv3, gmp/COPYINGv3.
  Source: https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gmp/gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz (SHA-256 GMP_SHA256), unmodified, pinned and built as FreeType
  is.

lsteamclient (lsteamclient.dll and lsteamclient.so: the Steam bridge, from Windows games' Steam API to Mac Steam's
steamclient.dylib)
  Licence: Valve's Steamworks SDK licence, lsteamclient/LICENSE (lsteamclient is Steamworks-SDK-derived); its cxx.h is
  LGPL-2.1-or-later (CodeWeavers, from Wine), lsteamclient/NOTE. It ships by the maintainer's decision of 2026-10-04
  under Valve's Steamworks SDK licence (lsteamclient/).
  Source: https://github.com/ValveSoftware/Proton.git, its lsteamclient/ folder at LSTEAMCLIENT_COMMIT (pinned in
  wine-arm64/deps.pins), with the patches in the repository's wine-arm64/patches/lsteamclient (dappermint/winecx's
  three Mac fixes).

DXVK 3.1.1 (the Direct3D to Vulkan DLLs in ../DXVK/aarch64-windows, for the games that render with DXVK)
  Licence: zlib, dxvk/LICENSE. Compiled in: dxbc-spirv (MIT), dxvk/dxbc-spirv-LICENSE; libdisplay-info (MIT),
  dxvk/libdisplay-info-LICENSE; the mingw-w64 DirectX headers, dxvk/directx-COPYING.MinGW-w64.txt; the SPIR-V headers,
  dxvk/spirv-headers-LICENSE; the Vulkan headers (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), dxvk/vulkan-headers-LICENSE.md.
  Source: https://github.com/doitsujin/dxvk.git at DXVK_COMMIT (tag v3.1.1; ../DXVK/version names it too) with its
  submodules at the DXVK_SUBMODULE_* commits, unmodified (pinned in wine-arm64/vulkan.pins).

KosmicKrisp (libvulkan_kosmickrisp.dylib: Mesa's Vulkan driver on Metal, which DXVK runs on)
  Licence: MIT, mesa/MIT; Mesa's overview of its licences, mesa/license.rst, and the other texts its sources name:
  mesa/Apache-2.0, mesa/BSL-1.0, mesa/SGI-B-2.0. xxHash (BSD-2-Clause) and Berkeley SoftFloat (BSD-3-Clause):
  NOTICES.md.
  Source: https://github.com/shadexternals/mesa.git at MESA_COMMIT, with the patches in the repository's
  wine-arm64/patches/mesa (pinned in wine-arm64/vulkan.pins).

The Vulkan loader (libvulkan.1.dylib, which Wine's winevulkan loads)
  Licence: Apache-2.0, vulkan-loader/LICENSE.txt. Built against the Vulkan headers (Apache-2.0 OR MIT):
  vulkan-headers/LICENSE.md, vulkan-headers/Apache-2.0.txt, vulkan-headers/MIT.txt.
  Source: https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Loader.git at VULKAN_LOADER_COMMIT and
  https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Headers.git at VULKAN_HEADERS_COMMIT, unmodified (pinned in
  wine-arm64/vulkan.pins).

MacNeutron (libmacneutron-present.dylib, the MetalFX presenter)
  Licence: MIT, macneutron/LICENSE.
  Source: the repository at MACNEUTRON_COMMIT: presenter/present.m. The patch files in wine-arm64/patches keep the
  licence of the tree they patch (Wine and DXMT: LGPL-2.1-or-later; FEX and KosmicKrisp: MIT; lsteamclient: Valve's
  terms).

